{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791195477,"nonce":"EM5JSrM1b1i3g4e9+guF4ZolHr0=","message":"Fixed in 65ddc47c0f94696e8bcb4a6b54d0ed59cec63a7b.\n\nNot state from earlier cases: testThreadRunWithEventLoop is the suite's first test, and `--ash-only` aborts too (threads.hl aborts while listing, so the isolated conformance tally never counted any threads case). ASH_TRACE_THROW shows the real throw underneath the ValueException:\n\n    Can't call closure whose type is not a function (closure=\u003cstack addr\u003e type kind=9 (HDYN) hasValue=0)\n\nlldb on hlp_error: hlp_value_to_string -\u003e buffer call_tostring_or_stub -\u003e worker_closure_runner -\u003e hlp_jit_closure_runner -\u003e hlp_call_method. call_tostring_or_stub builds a temporary vclosure typed hlt_dyn() for a `__string` that is still a stub sentinel. On the main thread the interpreter's runner ignores the type; since 9b848b4 (in v0.1.3) a worker lane's closure_runner is worker_closure_runner, which calls through hlp_call_method and needs a function type. The utest output path stringifies an object on the test's thread, which is how the suite reaches it.\n\nFix: on a worker lane, compile the stub (resolve_thread_root_sentinel, via fiber::compile_for_worker_lane) and call it like any compiled __string. call_closure_tostring_or_stub passes a real closure and was not affected; no other runtime site builds an hlt_dyn closure.\n\nReproducer test: crates/ash_cli/tests/worker_tostring.rs (WorkerToString.hx): old binary aborts under hybrid and jit, prints Named(worker) under interp; fixed binary prints it under all three.\nGates: threads and sys suites whole under interp/hybrid/jit all ok (1094/1094 assertions); parity_matrix, stdlib_matrix, shared_module_emitted, unresolved_helper pass.","files":null}]}